Looks like there are 38 instances of missing crop stage data; 4 days of missing "days since tillage" data; and 838 instances of missing VPD data.  I will use domain knowledge to fill in the gaps for the first two, and will need to impute VPD given its many missing values.

```{r}
# remove conventional field data after 10/1/2021, which is the last management data we have and accounts for the no-crop info; soybeans were harvested on this day and we have no management info for after that
cutoff_date <- as.Date("2021-10-01")  # example cutoff date

ec_daily_mngmnt3 <- ec_daily_mngmnt2 %>% 
  filter(!(management == "conventional" & date > cutoff_date))
# this brought us from 2805 to 2606, removing 199 rows of data.

# remove organic field data after 8/10/2021, as that's the last management data record we have for that field (the last date of alfalfa harvest) despite the records continuing into 2022
cutoff_date <- as.Date("2021-08-10")

ec_daily_mngmnt3 <- ec_daily_mngmnt3 %>% 
  filter(!(management == "organic" & date > cutoff_date))
# final number is 2407 observations, so that removed another two hundred or so from the organic side.

# write out and update:
write.csv(ec_daily_mngmnt3, "ecdaily_updateforalfalfaphenology.csv")
```

